# NewUnera Page Conversion — V1 → V2

Use this rule for every page that is being created or converted for the `NewUnera/` folder. The conversion is **design-only**: all functionality, copy, JS behavior, IDs, aria attributes, and link targets are preserved; only visual styling changes.

---

## 1. The Core Principle

> **Design only. Parity first.**
>
> Every conversion must produce a page in `NewUnera/` that is functionally and copy-wise **identical** to the source page. Styling is the only intended delta.

Never:
- Remove, skip, or simplify any form field, step, feature, JS function, or inline script block.
- Delete HTML comment blocks (e.g. commented social/wallet sections) — keep them as-is.
- Simplify or merge components because "they're not needed in V2."
- Omit any copy string: titles, subtitles, labels, hints, error messages, trust bars, CTA text, link text, modal titles/bodies, aria-labels, placeholders.

---

## 2. File Output

- **Always save converted pages to `NewUnera/`** — never overwrite root production files.
- `NewUnera/` is the single source of truth for all V2 pages.

---

## 3. Step-by-Step Conversion Checklist

Work through these steps in order. Each step has a verification note.

### Step 1 — Audit the source

Read the entire source file before changing anything. Note:
- All form IDs, `name`, `for`, `aria-*` attributes, `role` values.
- All `<script>` blocks and external script `src` paths.
- All external CSS `<link>` hrefs.
- All copy strings: every user-visible text node.
- All commented blocks.

### Step 2 — Typography

| V1 | V2 |
|----|-----|
| `<link>` to Google Fonts (Space Grotesk, Inter) | Remove the `<link>` tags entirely |
| Any `@font-face` for other fonts | Replace with V2 `@font-face` block |
| `font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif` | `font-family: var(--font-body)` |
| `font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif` | `font-family: var(--font-body)` |

**Required `@font-face` block** (copy from `NewUnera/dashboard-enhanced.html` lines 16–25 — ten OTF rules, `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-*.otf`):

```css
@font-face { font-family:'TestFoundersGrotesk'; src:url("../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Light.otf") format('opentype'); font-weight:300; font-style:normal; font-display:swap; }
@font-face { font-family:'TestFoundersGrotesk'; src:url("../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-LightItalic.otf") format('opentype'); font-weight:300; font-style:italic; font-display:swap; }
@font-face { font-family:'TestFoundersGrotesk'; src:url("../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Regular.otf") format('opentype'); font-weight:400; font-style:normal; font-display:swap; }
@font-face { font-family:'TestFoundersGrotesk'; src:url("../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-RegularItalic.otf") format('opentype'); font-weight:400; font-style:italic; font-display:swap; }
@font-face { font-family:'TestFoundersGrotesk'; src:url("../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Medium.otf") format('opentype'); font-weight:500; font-style:normal; font-display:swap; }
@font-face { font-family:'TestFoundersGrotesk'; src:url("../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-MediumItalic.otf") format('opentype'); font-weight:500; font-style:italic; font-display:swap; }
@font-face { font-family:'TestFoundersGrotesk'; src:url("../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Semibold.otf") format('opentype'); font-weight:600; font-style:normal; font-display:swap; }
@font-face { font-family:'TestFoundersGrotesk'; src:url("../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-SemiboldItalic.otf") format('opentype'); font-weight:600; font-style:italic; font-display:swap; }
@font-face { font-family:'TestFoundersGrotesk'; src:url("../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Bold.otf") format('opentype'); font-weight:700; font-style:normal; font-display:swap; }
@font-face { font-family:'TestFoundersGrotesk'; src:url("../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-BoldItalic.otf") format('opentype'); font-weight:700; font-style:italic; font-display:swap; }
```

Font stack tokens:
```css
--font-display: 'TestFoundersGrotesk', 'Oakes Grotesk', sans-serif;
--font-body:    'TestFoundersGrotesk', 'Oakes Grotesk', sans-serif;
```

Do NOT use `font-weight: 800` or `900` — maximum is `700`.

### Step 3 — CSS custom properties (`:root`)

Replace the entire `:root` block (or the V1 CSS `<link>` that provided it) with the canonical V2 `:root` copied from `NewUnera/dashboard-enhanced.html`. This includes:
- `--brand-*` color tokens
- Semantic alias tokens (`--primary-green`, `--neutral-*`, etc.)
- `--gradient-*` (solid/color-mix values — no CSS gradient functions on product HTML)
- `--fin-up`, `--fin-down`, `--fin-neutral` and their backgrounds
- `--success`, `--warning`, `--error`, `--error-bg`
- `--text-primary`, `--text-secondary`, `--border-subtle`, `--shadow-card`
- `--surface-*` tokens
- `--font-display`, `--font-body`

### Step 4 — External CSS dependencies

Remove any `<link rel="stylesheet">` to V1 CSS files (e.g. `auth-enhanced.css`, old component sheets). Replace with a self-contained `<style>` block in `<head>` using V2 tokens.

If the V1 external CSS provided utility classes used by JS (e.g. `.loading`, `.valid`, `.invalid`), re-implement those class selectors in the inline `<style>` block so JS still works.

### Step 5 — Script paths

Update `<script src="...">` paths that are relative and now incorrect from `NewUnera/`:

| V1 (from root) | V2 (from NewUnera/) |
|---|---|
| `src="auth-flow.js"` | `src="../auth-flow.js"` |
| `src="some-util.js"` | `src="../some-util.js"` |

Do NOT change any `window.location.href` values inside inline JS, `fetch()` URLs, or other runtime paths — these are behavior, not file references.

### Step 6 — Navigation / header

**Full app pages** (post-login, with DASHBOARD/WALLET/IMPACT links): Replace the V1 white nav with the V2 deep-blue nav. Copy the exact `<nav>` markup from `NewUnera/dashboard-enhanced.html` and update `aria-current` to reflect the active page.

**Pre-login / auth pages** (login, signup, forgot password): Use a simplified auth header:
- `background: var(--brand-deep-blue)`
- Logo: `<img src="NewLogo/Unera White Text Nav.svg" alt="UNERA" class="nav-logo-img" height="24">`
- Back button: white/75% text, hover → `var(--brand-yellow)`
- No nav links (user is not authenticated)

Logo rule — always use SVG files from `NewUnera/NewLogo/`:
- Dark header/nav: `NewLogo/Unera White Text Nav.svg`
- Light header: `NewLogo/Unera Black Text Nav.svg`
- Full wordmark (brand guide): `NewLogo/Unera White Text.svg` / `NewLogo/Unera Black Text.svg`
- Never use `../Brand Guide/Unera-Horizontal.png`

### Step 7 — Page background and body

```css
/* App pages */
body { background: var(--brand-white); }

/* Auth / pre-login pages */
body { background: var(--brand-cloud-blue); }
```

Never use a raw hex grey or V1 gradient for the body background.

### Step 8 — Cards

V2 card pattern (from `NewUnera/kyc-verify.html` `.widget-card`, `NewUnera/add-money.html`):

```css
.card, .widget-card, .auth-card {
    background: var(--brand-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    padding: 2rem;          /* or 2.5rem for auth cards */
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
}
```

Hover state (interactive cards):
```css
.card:hover {
    border-color: var(--brand-deep-blue);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(23, 61, 71, 0.15);
    transform: translateY(-4px);
}
```

### Step 9 — Buttons

| V1 pattern | V2 pattern |
|---|---|
| `.submit-btn` gradient green→blue | `background: var(--brand-deep-blue); color: var(--brand-white)` |
| `.btn-primary` gradient | `background: var(--brand-deep-blue); color: var(--brand-white)` |
| `background: linear-gradient(...)` on CTA | `background: var(--brand-deep-blue)` — no gradient functions |
| `.btn-secondary` (outline) | `background: transparent; border: 2px solid var(--border-subtle); color: var(--text-secondary)` |
| Min height 56px | Min height 46px |

All buttons: `min-height: 46px`, `font-family: var(--font-body)`, `border-radius: 0.75rem`.

Focus ring: `outline: 3px solid rgba(23, 61, 71, 0.30); outline-offset: 2px` on light surfaces.

Loading spinner: CSS `::after` pseudo-element with `border-top-color: var(--brand-white)`.
Success state: `background: var(--fin-up)`.

Keep all `id`, JS hooks (e.g. `loginBtn.classList.add('loading')`), and button text exactly as in source.

### Step 10 — Form inputs

```css
.form-input {
    border: 1.5px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    background: var(--brand-white);
}
.form-input:focus {
    border-color: var(--brand-deep-blue);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(23, 61, 71, 0.10);
    outline: none;
}
.form-input.invalid { border-color: var(--error); }
.form-input.valid   { border-color: var(--fin-up); }
```

Labels: `font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary)`.
Hints: `font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-secondary)`.
Errors: `font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--error)`.

On mobile (`max-width: 480px`): `font-size: 1rem` on all inputs to prevent iOS auto-zoom.

### Step 11 — Icons

Replace all V1 icon patterns with Material Symbols Outlined inline SVG per `.cursor/rules/newunera-icons.mdc`:
- `fill="currentColor"` on `<svg>` — never `stroke="currentColor"`
- `aria-hidden="true"` on decorative icons
- Sizing per the sizing table in the icons rule

V1 teal circle logo SVG → V2 Material lock/person/check icon in a `var(--brand-deep-blue)` chip.

Icon wells in auth: `width: 56px; height: 56px; border-radius: 1rem; background: var(--brand-deep-blue); color: var(--brand-white)`.

### Step 12 — Modals

Replace V1 gradient inline styles in modal overlays with V2 tokens:

```css
.modal-overlay { z-index: 10010; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.5); backdrop-filter: blur(4px); }
.modal { background: var(--brand-white); border-radius: 1.25rem; }
.modal-header { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); }
.modal-title { font-family: var(--font-display); color: var(--brand-deep-blue); }
```

Notification icon states:
- Default/info: `background: var(--brand-deep-blue); color: var(--brand-white)`
- Error: `background: var(--brand-red); color: var(--brand-white)`
- Warning: `background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-yellow) 55%, var(--brand-earth)); color: var(--brand-deep-blue)`

Keep the same show/hide JS mechanism (e.g. `style.display = 'flex'` vs `classList.add('active')`) as the source — do not change the modal trigger pattern.

### Step 13 — No CSS gradients

On product HTML (everything in `NewUnera/` except `brand-style-guide.html`):

```
❌ background: linear-gradient(...)
❌ background: radial-gradient(...)
❌ background: conic-gradient(...)
```

Replace with solid tokens:
```
✅ background: var(--brand-deep-blue)
✅ background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 50%, var(--brand-white))
✅ background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-yellow) 30%, var(--brand-white))
```

### Step 14 — Page titles

```css
/* V1: gradient clip text */
.page-title { background: var(--gradient-primary); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }

/* V2: solid deep-blue */
.page-title { color: var(--brand-deep-blue); font-weight: 700; }
```

### Step 15 — Accessibility

These are required on every converted page:

1. **Skip link** — first element in `<body>`:
   ```html
   <a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>
   ```
   ```css
   .skip-link { position:absolute; top:-40px; left:0; background:var(--brand-deep-blue); color:white; padding:8px 16px; text-decoration:none; z-index:10000; border-radius:0 0 8px 0; font-weight:600; }
   .skip-link:focus { top:0; outline:3px solid var(--brand-yellow); }
   ```

2. **Reduced motion**:
   ```css
   @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
       *, *::before, *::after {
           animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
           animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
           transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
       }
   }
   ```

3. **Focus rings** on interactive elements:
   - Light surfaces: `outline: 2px solid var(--brand-deep-blue); outline-offset: 2px`
   - Dark nav/header surfaces: `outline: 2px solid var(--brand-yellow); outline-offset: 2px`
   - Buttons: `outline: 3px solid rgba(23, 61, 71, 0.30); outline-offset: 2px`

4. **Preserve all** `aria-*`, `role`, `lang="en"`, `<label for>` bindings from source.

### Step 16 — Link and href paths

Adjust relative hrefs that are now incorrect from `NewUnera/`:

| Source target | V1 path (from root) | V2 path (from NewUnera/) |
|---|---|---|
| Root index | `index.html` | `../index.html` |
| Root auth page (e.g. forgot-password) | `forgot-password.html` | `../forgot-password.html` |
| Another NewUnera page | N/A | `other-page.html` (same folder, no `../`) |
| Anchor links | `#section` | `#section` (unchanged) |

Do NOT change `window.location.href` paths in inline JS (behavior, not markup).

### Step 17 — Responsive

Maintain the same breakpoints as the reference pages:

| Breakpoint | Required behavior |
|---|---|
| `≤ 768px` | Nav collapses to hamburger (app pages); auth card fills width; `btn-actions` → 1 column |
| `≤ 480px` | Compact layout; input `font-size: 1rem` (iOS zoom prevention); sticky CTA button |

